# id: BM17d-callsite-missing-from-list
# blinds: the fourth artifact of the correspondence, AllCallSites()
# covering-lane: cpp-scan
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# An enumerator drops out of the list the census iterates. Everything still
# compiles, every existing Env call still works, and the reachability census
# quietly stops looking for one call site -- so a genuinely unreachable Env call
# would be reported as fully covered. The failure the census exists to catch,
# arriving inside the census itself.
#
# NOT IN THE CATALOGUE. AllCallSites() was added at B1.3 because the census
# needs to iterate the enum, and a hand-written array beside a hand-written enum
# is a drift waiting to happen. Amendment A2 requires the mutant in the same
# change as the mechanism, so the list became the fourth thing cpp-scan binds by
# name and this is the patch that proves it is bound.
--- a/engine-cpp/src/env/call_site.cc	2026-08-24 17:51:25
+++ b/engine-cpp/src/env/call_site.cc	2026-08-24 17:51:25
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@
     CallSite::kEnvGetFileSize,
     CallSite::kEnvFileExists,
     CallSite::kEnvDeleteFile,
-    CallSite::kEnvRenameFile,
     CallSite::kEnvCreateDir,
     CallSite::kEnvLockFile,
     CallSite::kEnvUnlockFile,
